  "bodyTypst": "#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-ab-2002-form-b-frq-04-diagram-01.png\", width: 65%)\n\nThe graph of a differentiable function $f$ on the closed interval \\[-3, 15\\] is shown in the figure above. The graph of $f$ has a horizontal tangent line at $x = 6$. Let $g(x)= 5 + integral_(6)^(x) f(t) d t$ for $- 3 <= x <= 15$.\n\n(a) Find $g(6)\\, g'(6)$, and $g''(6)$.\n\n(b) On what intervals is $g$ decreasing? Justify your answer.\n\n(c) On what intervals is the graph of $g$ concave down? Justify your answer.\n\n(d) Find a trapezoidal approximation of $integral_(- 3)^(15) f(t) d t$ using six subintervals of length $Delta t = 3$.",
